<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  launchd LaunchAgent: keep the helper polling across logins and reboots.

  A TEMPLATE. `deploy/install-login-item.sh` fills in the three `__PLACEHOLDER__`
  values and loads it; nothing here hardcodes a username. Install by hand only
  if you want to read what you are installing first.

  This is the login item the launcher (docs/DesktopHelper.md, step 7) will
  eventually register for everyone else. It is written out here because the
  machine that needs it now is the one being developed on, and because a
  working reference beats writing it twice.

  Four things about it are decisions, not boilerplate:

  * It runs the INSTALLED tool (`~/.local/bin/gammonview-helper`), never
    `uv run` from a checkout. A login item aimed into a git working tree runs
    whatever branch happens to be checked out at boot, which is a debugging
    session nobody wants at 3am.

  * There is NO `Nice` key, and that is the opposite of the analysis worker's
    plist next door. `runner.lower_priority` calls `os.nice(cfg.nice)`, and
    POSIX `nice(2)` is an INCREMENT, not a level: launchd niceing the process
    to 10 and the helper then adding its own 10 lands it at 20, the floor of
    the scale. The helper nices itself; uvicorn does not. Set `nice` in
    `config.json` if you want to change it.

  * NO `ProcessType=Background`, for the reason the analysis plist records the
    measurement for: it forces the job onto E-cores with throttled I/O, which
    measured ~3.5x slower there. That would quietly undo the parallelism the
    helper now asks `gvanalysis` to size for it.

  * `KeepAlive` is unconditional, and `ThrottleInterval` now guards only real
    crashes. It used to guard a loop of our own making: the daemon exited 2
    when it had no credential, launchd restarted it, it exited again, and 60
    seconds was how long that stayed quiet. The cost showed up the day
    accounts went live -- `link` registers the worker with the site the
    instant you confirm it, so the throttle became the delay before a freshly
    paired machine did any work, and the first analysis on gammonview.com sat
    queued 31 of its 36 seconds. The daemon waits in-process for a credential
    now (`daemon.wait_for_token`), so there is no loop left to damp and no
    `launchctl kickstart` for a user to know about.

  Manage:
    launchctl bootout   gui/$(id -u)/com.gammonview.helper     # stop + forget
    launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.gammonview.helper  # restart
    tail -f __LOG_DIR__/helper.log
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.gammonview.helper</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>__HELPER_BIN__</string>
        <string>run</string>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <!-- Explicit even though `config.py` now defaults to the same site.
             A login item is the one copy of this setting a person can find
             without reading Python, and it is what `install-login-item.sh`
             reads back so that re-running it does not move an installed helper
             between sites. Point a second machine at beta by installing with
             GAMMONVIEW_SITE set. -->
        <key>GAMMONVIEW_SITE</key>
        <string>__SITE__</string>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- 10s is launchd's default and is too eager for a helper that exits
         because the site said no. -->
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__LOG_DIR__/helper.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__LOG_DIR__/helper.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
